# Vulnerabilities deliberately not fixed yet, for the image scan in the `image`
# job of .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT BELONGS HERE, AND WHAT DOES NOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The gate is HIGH and CRITICAL with `ignore-unfixed: true`. So a finding with
# no published fix never reaches this file — it is reported in the log by the
# preceding step and cannot be acted on, and failing the build on it would make
# the check permanently red for a reason nobody in this repository can resolve.
#
# This file is therefore only for the narrow case of a **fixable** finding that
# is deliberately being deferred. That is a decision, so every entry needs:
#
#   * the CVE id
#   * the date it was added
#   * the issue tracking the fix
#   * one line on why it is safe to defer, specific to how this image uses it
#
# An entry with no expiry is how a suppression outlives the reason for it, so
# prefer `# expires: YYYY-MM-DD` and treat a passed date as a bug.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT THE PLACE FOR A BASE IMAGE BUMP
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If the fix is "take a newer base image", the answer is to bump the pinned tag
# in the Dockerfile — `ARG NODE_VERSION` / `ARG GO_VERSION` / `ARG
# RUNTIME_DIGEST` — which is Dependabot's job (#22) and arrives as a commit
# somebody reviewed. Adding the CVE here instead trades a reviewed bump for a
# silent one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/web
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-14456 — libssl3 / libcrypto3 3.5.7-r0, fixed in 3.5.8-r0.
#
# added:    2026-08-28
# issue:    #145
# expires:  2026-11-28
#
# Fixable in Alpine and not by any change this repository can make. The web
# image pins NODE_VERSION=22.23.2 on alpine3.24, and the floating
# `node:22-alpine3.24` tag currently resolves to that same 22.23.2 carrying
# libssl3-3.5.7-r0 — so bumping the pin fixes nothing. Verified rather than
# assumed:
#
#     docker run --rm node:22-alpine3.24 apk list --installed | grep libssl3
#     libssl3-3.5.7-r0
#
# `RUN apk upgrade` in the runtime stage would fix it today and is deliberately
# not taken: it makes the same Dockerfile produce a different image on different
# days, which contradicts the pinning argument both Dockerfiles state in their
# own comments. #145 carries that judgement call and the removal condition.
#
# The Next server does not expose this library to untrusted input directly — its
# TLS is terminated at the load balancer — which is why deferring is acceptable
# rather than merely convenient.
CVE-2026-14456

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/api
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nothing. Distroless carries no package manager and no userland, and the Go
# stdlib findings that were present when this gate was written (8 fixable HIGH
# CVEs against 1.26.5) were fixed the way findings are supposed to be fixed —
# by bumping ARG GO_VERSION to 1.26.6 in the same PR, not by an entry here.
